---
// Privacy Policy. Required before AdSense review: Google's programme policies
// oblige every publisher to disclose the use of advertising cookies, name the
// third-party vendors involved, and tell visitors how to opt out.
//
// The body is in English and says so: legal terms translate badly, and a
// mistranslated liability or consent clause is worse than an honest note that
// the English text governs. Headings carry Sinhala alongside.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro'

const UPDATED = '11 September 2026'
const CONTACT = 'tilershub@gmail.com'
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy · TilersHub"
  description="How TilersHub collects, uses and protects your data — including cookies, analytics and advertising partners."
>
  <div style="background:var(--navy);padding:48px 20px 40px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;">
      <h1 style="font-family:var(--th-display);font-size:clamp(26px,5vw,40px);font-weight:800;color:#fff;margin:0 0 10px;line-height:1.15;">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p style="font-size:14px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.6);margin:0;">
        <span class="si-text">පෞද්ගලිකත්ව ප්‍රතිපත්තිය · </span>Last updated {UPDATED}
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="legal">
    <p class="lede">
      TilersHub (“we”, “us”) operates <strong>tilershub.lk</strong>, a free marketplace that connects
      homeowners in Sri Lanka with tilers, contractors, tile shops, brands and suppliers. This policy
      explains what we collect, why, who we share it with, and the choices you have.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      <span class="si-text">මෙම ප්‍රතිපත්තිය ඉංග්‍රීසි බසින් ලියා ඇත. නීතිමය අර්ථය සඳහා ඉංග්‍රීසි පිටපත බලපායි. ප්‍රශ්න ඇත්නම් අප හා සම්බන්ධ වන්න.</span>
      <span class="en-text">Questions about anything below? Email us at {CONTACT} — we answer in English or Sinhala.</span>
    </p>

    <h2>1. Information you give us</h2>
    <p>We only ask for what a job actually needs:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Posting a project</strong> — your name, WhatsApp number, district and city, and the description, budget and photos of the work. No account is required.</li>
      <li><strong>Sending a quote</strong> — your name, WhatsApp number, quoted price, timeline and message.</li>
      <li><strong>Registering as a provider</strong> — your business name, service type, districts covered, services offered, contact numbers, description and photographs of past work.</li>
      <li><strong>Signing in</strong> — if you choose to sign in with Google, we receive your email address and account identifier from Google. We never see or store your Google password.</li>
      <li><strong>Reviews</strong> — the rating, review text and the name you choose to publish it under.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. Information collected automatically</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Usage data</strong> — pages visited, referring site, approximate location derived from your IP address, device type and browser, collected through Google Analytics via Google Tag Manager.</li>
      <li><strong>Local storage</strong> — your chosen language and district are stored in your own browser so the site remembers them. This never leaves your device and we cannot read it.</li>
      <li><strong>Cookies</strong> — see section 5.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>3. How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To show your project to providers who work in your area, so they can quote.</li>
      <li>To show provider listings, ratings and reviews to homeowners searching for work.</li>
      <li>To let you sign in and manage your own projects, quotes and listing.</li>
      <li>To review provider applications before they are published.</li>
      <li>To understand which pages and services are useful, and to fix what is not.</li>
      <li>To detect and prevent fraud, spam and abuse of the platform.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information to anyone.</p>

    <h2>4. Who your information is shared with</h2>
    <p class="callout">
      <strong>Posting a project shares your contact details.</strong> When you post a project, the
      name and WhatsApp number you provide are shown to registered providers so they can contact you
      about it. This is the whole point of the service — but it means you should not include anything
      in a project description you would not want a tradesperson to read.
    </p>
    <p>Beyond that, we share data only with the service providers that make the site work:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong> — database, file storage and authentication.</li>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — website hosting and delivery.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> — Analytics, Tag Manager, Sign-in, and advertising (see section 5).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may also disclose information where the law requires it, or where it is necessary to protect
      the rights and safety of our users.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Cookies and advertising</h2>
    <p>A cookie is a small file a website stores in your browser. We use:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Essential cookies</strong> — to keep you signed in. The site cannot work without these.</li>
      <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> — Google Analytics, to count visits and see which pages are used. Only set if you accept.</li>
      <li><strong>Advertising cookies</strong> — set by Google and its partners if advertising is shown on the site. Only set if you accept.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on your prior visits to
      this website or other websites. Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners
      to serve ads to you based on your visit to this site and/or other sites on the internet.
    </p>
    <p>You can turn this off at any time:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Opt out of personalised advertising by Google at
        <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">google.com/settings/ads</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Opt out of other third-party vendors at
        <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">aboutads.info/choices</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Read how Google uses data from sites that use its services at
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        Change your choice on this site at any time using the button at the bottom of this page.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      You can also block or delete cookies in your browser settings. Blocking essential cookies will
      sign you out and stop parts of the site working.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Keeping your information</h2>
    <p>
      Projects, quotes, reviews and provider listings stay on the site while they are useful to other
      users. You can ask us to delete your account and the content attached to it at any time by
      emailing {CONTACT} from the address you signed up with; we action requests within 30 days.
      Some records may be kept longer where the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Ask for a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      <li>Ask us to correct anything that is wrong — provider listings can also be edited yourself from your account.</li>
      <li>Ask us to delete your account and content.</li>
      <li>Withdraw consent for analytics and advertising cookies.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Email {CONTACT} for any of these.</p>

    <h2>8. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The site is served over HTTPS, and access to the database is restricted by row-level security
      rules so users can only reach their own records. No system is perfectly secure, so please do not
      send bank details, ID numbers or passwords through project descriptions or quote messages.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Children</h2>
    <p>
      TilersHub is not intended for anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect information from
      children. If you believe a child has given us information, email {CONTACT} and we will remove it.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Provider listings, brand pages and guides may link to other websites and to WhatsApp. We are not
      responsible for the privacy practices of those sites — read their policies before sharing
      anything.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes we will update the date at the top of this page. Significant changes will
      be announced on the site.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      TilersHub · Sri Lanka<br />
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT}`}>{CONTACT}</a><br />
      WhatsApp: <a href="https://wa.me/94774503744" target="_blank" rel="noopener">+94 77 450 3744</a>
    </p>

    <div class="consent-reset">
      <button id="reset-consent" type="button" class="btn btn-outline">Change my cookie choice</button>
      <span id="reset-done" hidden style="font-size:13px;color:var(--green);font-weight:600;">Saved — reloading…</span>
    </div>
  </article>

  <script is:inline>
    document.getElementById('reset-consent')?.addEventListener('click', function () {
      try { localStorage.removeItem('th_consent') } catch (e) {}
      document.getElementById('reset-done').hidden = false
      setTimeout(function () { location.reload() }, 600)
    })
  </script>
</Layout>
